  "readmeFile": "readme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.6.0: enums describe themselves in a template: Format, FormatByName and FormatParams read an enum or IDescribable argument by Describe's letters ({0} its words, {0:T} its tooltip, {0:D} its number), and Words.ToDescribe does the same for string.Format and interpolated strings (string.Create(Words.ToDescribe, $\"{brew:T}\")); a provider's own ICustomFormatter still sees each argument first, the enum as it is. Describe reads what the app registers on the builder, ConfigureDescribe(d => d.Fill/FillKey/Keys/Slot), frozen into each dictionary (IWords.DescribeRegistry), so an app keeps its own attributes, keys an enum it does not own, or adds a slot; a subclassed [Description] reads as its base. One pass for every brace: a value is read once (WordsTemplate.Parse), and Words fills its format items itself, so nothing a value says makes Format throw: an item with nothing to read shows #{3}# or #{Name}# (WORDS:FIELD), a format its argument rejects #{0}# (WORDS:FORMAT), a brace that opens nothing shows as written (WORDS:FORMAT), and a name may take an alignment. Fixed: words an IWords of your own answers that select their own forms are cut as circular, and Debug marks a fraction's missing other. Upgrading: an enum in a template printed its member name, and now prints its words, else its [Description], else its name; {0:d} is the description, and Enum's X, F and g are no slot, shown marked #!X# with a WORDS:SLOT warning (pass ToString() for Enum's own text). Describe's D is the number, where it was the description; i and n are retired; U is no longer built in (ConfigureDescribe(d => d.Slot('U', \".unit\")) brings it back); and a value with an obsolete alias reads its first name that is not obsolete. Braces: {{ is one brace, formatted or not, and }} two, in a value or a template handed to FormatByName or PreFormatByName; a constant's words are text, so its {0} shows as written; \\\\, '' and \"\" in a value read as written, collapsed once by the file reader where rendering collapsed them again; a reference in a format item ({0:{>fmt}}) and a lone { show as written with a warning, and a number past the arguments or a rejected format show marked, where Format threw; a name no member answers shows #{Name}# where it showed #Name#; and a selector past the arguments picks other, with a warning. FormatByName reads a public field or a property with a public getter and no index. IWords gains DescribeRegistry, with a default: an IWords wrapping another passes the inner one's on.",
